        section("Operations and mathematical guarantees", "Free identity/compose/inverse/between/act wrappers delegate to static policy methods. between defaults to inverse(a)*b when a specialized method is absent. Group interpolate uses a specialized method or a*exp(t*log(a^-1*b)); non-group interpolate uses exp_map(p,t*log_map(p,q)). geodesic requires a base-point exp_map and is not automatically supplied by the one-argument Lie-group exponential.",
                "Concept satisfaction checks a subset of expressions, not every wrapper or mathematical axiom. Some policy methods intentionally provide approximations under standard names: Stiefel exp/log/parallel transport and several inverse retractions are specified in their type entries. Input points must satisfy unit, orthogonality, positivity, or group invariants unless explicitly projected; no universal validity checker or status result is supplied."),
        section("Storage, lifetime, and concurrency", "Embedded manifold policies have static functions and no owned point state. Point/tangent vec/mat values and concrete Lie-group members own fixed inline arrays/scalars; copying is proportional to stored extent, and operations use fixed automatic scratch rather than a heap. Matrix decompositions can require full N-by-N working matrices even when a point has only P columns. No allocator or runtime workspace parameter is exposed here.",
                "Methods do not retain references or maintain mutable caches. Separate result/output storage supports concurrent read-only use of valid points and group values. Mutation requires synchronization. Borrowed batch views retain only addresses and require caller-controlled extents/lifetimes; destruction or relocation of the arrays invalidates them. No iterators are provided."),
        section("Lie-algebra helpers", "hat_so3 maps a three-vector to its 3x3 cross-product skew matrix; vee_so3 extracts entries [2,1],[0,2],[1,0] without checking skew symmetry. hat_se3 embeds the translation-first six-vector in a 4x4 algebra matrix; vee_se3 extracts the corresponding six entries without checking the homogeneous row. These fixed conversions cost O(1). hat_son and vee_son are identity matrix copies, O(N²), rather than compact coordinate packing or skew projection.",
                "lie_bracket(X,Y)=X*Y-Y*X performs two dense products, O(N³) work and O(N²) temporary storage. algebra_exp/algebra_log accept general square matrices and do not enforce Lie-algebra/group membership; their output follows the underlying real matrix-function algorithm and diagnostic checks."),
        section("Numerical limits and diagnostics", "Specialized low-dimensional methods use fixed small-angle polynomials and transcendental formulas, with no user convergence tolerance. SVD/eigensystem/matrix-function wrappers use their underlying fixed defaults and often discard convergence/existence flags. Invalid or rank-deficient data can therefore yield a numeric fallback or NaNs without a manifold status object.",
                "Sphere antipodal logarithms and invalid hyperbolic projections report domain_error through micron::exc. Generic Lie algebra_exp/algebra_log check the matrix-function flags only when hosted exceptions or the micron EH configuration enable their guarded checks; bare freestanding calls return the computed result matrix without those checks. The exception/noexcept behavior of these entry points follows the configured exception support."),
